window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"memories\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">记忆</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 和 Codex 可以把先前工作中的有用上下文带入后续工作。ChatGPT 网页版使用 ChatGPT 记忆；本地 Codex 客户端使用另一套独立的本地记忆存储和控制项。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>必须始终遵循的团队指引应放在 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或已纳入版本控制的文档中。记忆只是便于回想信息的辅助层，不应成为必须始终遵守的规则的唯一来源。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，使用 <code>/memories</code> 选择聊天是否可以使用本地记忆，或是否可以为后续记忆提供素材。在<strong>设置 &gt; 个性化（Settings &gt; Personalization）</strong>中，使用<strong>启用 Codex 记忆（Enable Codex memories）</strong>为所选机器启用或停用此功能。使用<strong>允许来自工具辅助聊天的记忆（Allow memories from tool-assisted chats）</strong>，选择使用过 MCP 工具或网页搜索的聊天是否可以为后续记忆提供素材。</p> <p>若要重置所选机器的记忆存储，请选择<strong>删除 Codex 记忆（Delete Codex memories）</strong>并确认。如果操作对象是本地机器，且电脑使用历史（Computer History）功能可用，此操作也会清除电脑使用历史。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在<strong>设置 &gt; 个性化</strong>中管理 ChatGPT 记忆。ChatGPT Work 使用你的账户和工作区可用的记忆设置；它不使用本地 Codex 记忆存储或本地记忆控制项。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 Codex CLI 的交互式会话中，使用 <code>/memories</code> 控制当前聊天是否可以使用已有的本地记忆，或是否可以为未来记忆提供素材。如果没有该命令，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc?anchor=configure-local-memories\">配置本地记忆</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>IDE 扩展使用所连接 Codex 主机的本地记忆存储。为该主机启用记忆后，可像在 Codex CLI 中一样使用聊天级控制项。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">电脑使用历史</a>是 macOS 桌面功能。它会将允许访问的应用和网站中的活动整理成记忆和时间线，供 ChatGPT 与 Codex 参考。</p> <p><a id=\"how-memories-work\"></a> <a id=\"memory-storage\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-thread\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-chat\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-task\"></a> <a id=\"review-memories\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-local-codex-memories-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">本地 Codex 记忆如何工作</h2> <p>启用记忆后，Codex 可以将符合条件的历史聊天中的有用上下文整理为本地记忆文件。Codex 会跳过仍在活动中或生命周期较短的会话，会从生成的记忆字段中删除密钥，并在后台更新记忆，而不是在每次聊天结束时立即更新。</p> <p>聊天结束后，记忆不一定会马上更新。Codex 会等待聊天闲置足够长的时间，以免总结仍在进行中的工作。</p> <p>如果 Codex 的剩余速率限制低于配置的阈值，记忆生成也可能跳过一次后台处理，从而避免在额度接近用尽时消耗配额。</p> <p><a id=\"local-memory-storage\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">本地记忆存储位置</h2> <p>Codex 会将记忆保存在 Codex 主目录中。默认主目录为 <code>~/.codex</code>。有关 <code>CODEX_HOME</code> 的使用方式，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=config-and-state-locations\">配置与状态目录</a>。</p> <p>主要记忆文件位于 <code>~/.codex/memories/</code> 下，包括摘要、长期保留的条目、近期输入以及来自先前聊天的支持证据。</p> <p>请将这些文件视为自动生成的状态数据。排查问题或准备分享 Codex 主目录之前，你可以检查这些文件；但不要把手动编辑它们当作主要控制方式。</p> <p><a id=\"control-local-memories-per-task\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"control-local-memories-per-chat\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">按聊天控制本地记忆</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用和 Codex TUI 中，使用 <code>/memories</code> 控制当前聊天的记忆行为。聊天级选项可以决定当前聊天是否能使用现有记忆，以及 Codex 是否可以使用当前聊天来生成未来记忆。</p> <p>聊天级选择不会更改全局记忆设置。</p> <p><a id=\"review-local-memories\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">查看本地记忆</h2> <p>不要将密钥保存在记忆中。Codex 会从自动生成的记忆字段中删除密钥，但在分享 Codex 主目录或自动生成的记忆文件之前，你仍应检查文件内容。</p> <p><a id=\"enable-memories\"></a> <a id=\"configuration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"configure-local-memories\">配置本地记忆</h2> <p>本地 Codex 记忆默认处于关闭状态。在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，打开<strong>设置 &gt; 个性化（Settings &gt; Personalization）</strong>并启用<strong>启用 Codex 记忆（Enable Codex memories）</strong>。</p> <p>也可以通过配置文件启用功能标志，在 <code>config.toml</code> 中添加：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\nmemories = true\n</code></pre> <p>有关配置文件位置和所有记忆相关设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>常见的记忆专用设置包括：</p> <ul> <li><code>memories.generate_memories</code>：控制新建的聊天是否可以作为记忆生成的输入。</li> <li><code>memories.use_memories</code>：控制 Codex 是否会将已有记忆注入未来的会话。</li> <li><code>memories.disable_on_external_context</code>：设为 <code>true</code> 时，使用过 MCP 工具调用、网页搜索或工具搜索等外部上下文的聊天不会用于生成记忆。旧键 <code>memories.no_memories_if_mcp_or_web_search</code> 仍可作为兼容别名使用。</li> <li><code>memories.min_rate_limit_remaining_percent</code>：设置开始生成记忆所需的 Codex 速率限制最低剩余百分比。</li> <li><code>memories.extract_model</code>：覆盖用于提取单个聊天记忆的模型。</li> <li><code>memories.consolidation_model</code>：覆盖用于汇总整理全局记忆的模型。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"memories\">Memories</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Memories let ChatGPT and Codex carry useful context from earlier work into future work. ChatGPT web uses ChatGPT memory, while local Codex clients use a separate local memory store and controls.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Keep required team guidance in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or checked-in documentation. Treat memories as a helpful recall layer, not as the only source for rules that must always apply.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, use <code>/memories</code> to choose whether a chat can use local memories or contribute to future memories. In <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization</strong>, use <strong>Enable Codex memories</strong> to turn the feature on or off for the selected machine. Use <strong>Allow memories from tool-assisted chats</strong> to choose whether chats that use MCP tools or web search can contribute to future memories.</p> <p>To reset the selected machine's memory store, select <strong>Delete Codex memories</strong> and confirm. On the local machine, this also clears Computer History when that feature is available.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Manage ChatGPT memory from <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization</strong>. ChatGPT Work uses the memory settings available to your account and workspace; it doesn't use a local Codex memory store or local memory controls.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In Codex CLI, use <code>/memories</code> in an interactive session to control whether the current chat can use existing local memories or become an input for future memories. See <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc?anchor=configure-local-memories\">Configure local memories</a> if the command isn't available.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The IDE extension uses the connected Codex host's local memory store. When memories are enabled for that host, use the same chat-level controls as Codex CLI.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a> is a macOS desktop feature that turns activity across allowed apps and websites into memories and a timeline that ChatGPT and Codex can reference.</p> <p><a id=\"how-memories-work\"></a> <a id=\"memory-storage\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-thread\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-chat\"></a> <a id=\"control-memories-per-task\"></a> <a id=\"review-memories\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-local-codex-memories-work\">How local Codex memories work</h2> <p>After you enable memories, Codex can turn useful context from eligible prior chats into local memory files. Codex skips active or short-lived sessions, redacts secrets from generated memory fields, and updates memories in the background instead of immediately at the end of every chat.</p> <p>Memories may not update right away when a chat ends. Codex waits until a chat has been idle long enough to avoid summarizing work that's still in progress.</p> <p>Memory generation can also skip a background pass when your Codex rate-limit remaining percentage is below the configured threshold, so Codex doesn't spend quota when you're near a limit.</p> <h2 id=\"local-memory-storage\">Local memory storage</h2> <p>Codex stores memories under your Codex home directory. By default, that's <code>~/.codex</code>. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=config-and-state-locations\">Config and state locations</a> for how Codex uses <code>CODEX_HOME</code>.</p> <p>The main memory files live under <code>~/.codex/memories/</code> and include summaries, durable entries, recent inputs, and supporting evidence from prior chats.</p> <p>Treat these files as generated state. You can inspect them when troubleshooting or before sharing your Codex home directory, but don't rely on editing them by hand as your primary control surface.</p> <p><a id=\"control-local-memories-per-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"control-local-memories-per-chat\">Control local memories per chat</h2> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app and Codex TUI, use <code>/memories</code> to control memory behavior for the current chat. Chat-level choices let you decide whether the current chat can use existing memories and whether Codex can use the chat to generate future memories.</p> <p>Chat-level choices don't change your global memory settings.</p> <h2 id=\"review-local-memories\">Review local memories</h2> <p>Don't store secrets in memories. Codex redacts secrets from generated memory fields, but you should still review memory files before sharing your Codex home directory or generated memory artifacts.</p> <p><a id=\"enable-memories\"></a> <a id=\"configuration\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"configure-local-memories\">Configure local memories</h2> <p>Local Codex memories are off by default. In the ChatGPT desktop app, open <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization</strong> and turn on <strong>Enable Codex memories</strong>.</p> <p>For config-based setup, add the feature flag to <code>config.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\nmemories = true\n</code></pre> <p>For config file locations and the full list of memory-related settings, see <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a> and the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">configuration reference</a>.</p> <p>Common memory-specific settings include:</p> <ul> <li><code>memories.generate_memories</code>: controls whether newly created chats can be stored as memory-generation inputs.</li> <li><code>memories.use_memories</code>: controls whether Codex injects existing memories into future sessions.</li> <li><code>memories.disable_on_external_context</code>: when <code>true</code>, keeps chats that used external context such as MCP tool calls, web search, or tool search out of memory generation. The older <code>memories.no_memories_if_mcp_or_web_search</code> key is still accepted as an alias.</li> <li><code>memories.min_rate_limit_remaining_percent</code>: controls the minimum remaining Codex rate-limit percentage required before memory generation starts.</li> <li><code>memories.extract_model</code>: overrides the model used for per-chat memory extraction.</li> <li><code>memories.consolidation_model</code>: overrides the model used for global memory consolidation.</li> </ul>"};
